\details{
Three models of the paper are special cases:
\itemize{
\item \eqn{\mathcal{M}_0}{M0}: \code{D = 0}, \code{link = "none"}, a DyNAM with random
activity effects and no latent positions;
\item \eqn{\mathcal{M}_1}{M1}: \code{D >= 1}, \code{link = "none"}, the latent space
DyNAM without link;
\item \eqn{\mathcal{M}_2}{M2}: \code{D >= 1} with a link, by default the additive
link in latent popularity and excess self-affinity, \code{c("pop", "rho")}.
}

With \code{inference = "mcmc"} both stages are simulated by MALA, with the
summaries plugged in at the posterior means of the aligned positions. With
\code{inference = "map"} both stages use the Laplace approximation at the
posterior mode: this is fast, but the summaries are plugged in at the mode,
which attenuates the link when actors have few events. The analysis of the
paper used \code{inference = "mcmc"}, \code{n_iter = 12000}, \code{burn_in = 2000},
\code{thin = 5}, \code{n_starts = 30} and \code{n_cut = 300}.
